Q: Why does {.tabset} not work with htmltools::tagList? A: <p>This has been answered in <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/63495651/28479453">Leaflet not rendering in dynamically generated R markdown html knitr</a> or conceptually in <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79667255/28479453">Ggplotly doesn't work in asis result Quarto</a> and these can be applied to your problem like</p>
<pre><code>---
title: &quot;test&quot;
output: html_document
---

```{r setup, include=FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(echo = FALSE)
library(leaflet)
# Init Step to make sure that the dependencies are loaded
leaflet()
ranges &lt;- paste0(&quot;section_&quot;, c(1:3))
```


```{r echo=FALSE, results='asis'}
cat(&quot;## Tabs {.tabset}&quot;, &quot;\n&quot;)
for (i in seq_along(ranges)) {
  cat(&quot;### Number&quot;, i, &quot;\n&quot;)
  cat(&quot;\n\n\n&quot;)

  htmltools::tagList(
    leaflet() |&gt;
       addTiles() |&gt;
       addProviderTiles(&quot;OpenStreetMap&quot;, group = &quot;OSM&quot;) |&gt;
       addLayersControl(baseGroups = c(&quot;OSM&quot;, &quot;Toner Lite&quot;)) |&gt;
       addCircleMarkers(lat = 47, lng = 9, popup = ranges[i])
    ) |&gt;
    as.character() |&gt;
    cat()
}
```
